A||N||14||stimpy||It's alive, ALIVE!!!||||14||
Z||000000||stimpy||09-10-2001||08:40 AM||||Well, here's the update for this thread... <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013085.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013085.html</A> <BR>After replacing the belt, I found out my 4th alternator since March had sh!t the bed. I replaced it again, just to find that the casing on #5 was stripped where the adjustment bolt goes in. Out comes #5, I go to O'Reilly's and get my money back. (To their credit, they were cool about it, just have crappy alternators.)<BR>On to Napa, where I scored a 94 amp alternator. By now, I'm getting the hang of this alternator swapping (thank God it's not an automatic!) and do the job in about 20 minutes this time.<P>Moment of truth... I turn the key and she fires right up purring like a nasty kitten. No leaks, no smoking, no loss of acceleration.<BR>The Fiero gods are appeased!<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000001||JohnF||09-10-2001||08:44 AM||||FYI - my '88 has stayed with the original GM/Delco unit as recommended by my (very) trusted mechanic because they had had a lot of trouble with 3rd party rebuilts and the rebuilders.  At 120k+, I have just started my 3rd alt.||||reg||11
Z||000002||87GTZ34||09-10-2001||08:50 AM||||Stimpy, Glad to hear your car didn't bite it.  I would run your fresh oil change for just a few hundred miles and then change again with prolong or slick50 and use that until the next oil change.  That will help to get out any wear material that was prematurely caused from the excessive heat and also any sludge that was knocked loose from it.  The prolong or slick50 will help newly exposed metal surfaces in friction areas and lifters/valve train. GL||||reg||1
Z||000003||SteveJ||09-10-2001||09:19 AM||||"prolong or slick50 " <P>None of their claims can be reproduced in the lab.<P>Both are having action taken against them for false and misleading advertizing. Don't see any ads for them any more do you.<P>Keep that crap out of your car it upsets the additive package that the original oil has.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.phoenixknights.net/teamsc3/articles/aftermarketbs01.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.phoenixknights.net/teamsc3/articles/aftermarketbs01.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||1
