Z||000009||Cheever3000||09-10-2001||06:52 PM||||Thanks for the tip!  Mine is whining, and if/when I get the dough, I <B>was</B> going to get it at O'Reilly's.  You saved me some grief.  Sorry to hear somebody couldn't have done the same for you.<P>I'm curious what NAPA's costed you.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000010||stimpy||09-10-2001||07:03 PM||||The Napa alt was $64 + tax, basically same as the O'Reilly's.<BR>The O'Reilly's has a lifetime warranty where the Napa's is 3 years, but I'd rather have an alternator for 3 years then be swapping them every month for the rest of my life!<P>Oh, and make sure you use Gates brand belts! Definately worth the extra couple of bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000011||beer_stud_21||09-10-2001||08:53 PM||||$64.00!! I recently bought a (i believe it was) 120amp alt for an 89 T-bird.  came to something like 130 AFTER i got back 33 for the core...  That was at napa too.  This is the third alt I've put in this car.  The other two wern't from napa tho, so this one with a 3 yr waranty had better last 2 yrs and 11 months!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-marlin||||reg||1
